          "action": {
            "library": "H5P.MultiChoice 1.16",
            "params": {
              "question": "<p>According to the 2024 Lancet Commission, what is the single largest modifiable risk factor for dementia?</p>",
              "answers": [
                {
                  "text": "<div>Hypertension</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Hypertension is a well-recognised modifiable risk factor for dementia, but the 2024 Lancet Commission identified a sensory deficit — not a cardiovascular one — as the single largest contributor.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Physical inactivity</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Physical inactivity contributes to dementia risk, but the 2024 Lancet Commission named a sensory deficit, not a lifestyle factor, as the largest modifiable risk factor.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Hearing loss</div>",
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Correct. The 2024 Lancet Commission identified hearing loss as the single largest modifiable risk factor for dementia, reframing every hearing aid conversation as brain protection rather than just convenience.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Diabetes mellitus</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Diabetes mellitus is a known risk factor for both vascular and Alzheimer-type dementia, but the 2024 Lancet Commission specifically highlighted hearing loss as the largest modifiable risk factor.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                }
              ],
              "overallFeedback": [
                {
                  "from": 0,
                  "to": 50,
                  "feedback": "The 2024 Lancet Commission named hearing loss as the single largest modifiable risk factor for dementia. This reframes hearing aid use as a form of brain protection, not merely a quality-of-life measure."
                },
                {
                  "from": 51,
                  "to": 100,
                  "feedback": "Well done. This finding transforms how we counsel elderly patients about hearing aids — it is not just about social convenience but about actively protecting cognitive function."
                }
              ],
              "behaviour": {
