          },
          "pause": true,
          "displayType": "poster",
          "buttonOnMobile": false,
          "label": "<p>When reviewing Krishnamurthy's eight medications prescribed by different special</p>",
          "x": 30,
          "y": 30,
          "width": 40,
          "height": 25,
          "libraryTitle": "Multiple Choice",
          "action": {
            "library": "H5P.MultiChoice 1.16",
            "params": {
              "question": "<p>When reviewing Krishnamurthy's eight medications prescribed by different specialists, which tools would you use to identify medications that should be stopped or started?</p>",
              "answers": [
                {
                  "text": "<div>The Mini Nutritional Assessment (MNA)</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>The MNA screens for malnutrition risk in older adults. It does not evaluate medication appropriateness. Polypharmacy management requires dedicated pharmacological review tools.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>The Beers Criteria and STOPP/START criteria</div>",
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Correct. The Beers Criteria identify potentially inappropriate medications in older adults, while the STOPP/START criteria flag both medications that should be stopped and those being wrongly omitted. Together they guide the goal of achieving the simplest effective regimen.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>The Confusion Assessment Method (CAM)</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>The CAM screens for delirium. While medications can cause delirium, the tool for systematic medication review in the elderly is the Beers Criteria and STOPP/START criteria.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>The Geriatric Depression Scale (GDS-15)</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>The GDS-15 screens for depression in older adults. While certain medications can worsen mood, the dedicated tools for polypharmacy review are the Beers Criteria and STOPP/START criteria.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                }
              ],
              "overallFeedback": [
                {
                  "from": 0,
                  "to": 50,
                  "feedback": "The Beers Criteria and STOPP/START criteria are the standard tools for polypharmacy management in older adults. They help identify medications to stop (potentially inappropriate) and medications to start (being wrongly withheld)."
                },
                {
                  "from": 51,
                  "to": 100,
                  "feedback": "Well done. In geriatric management, the goal is not to follow every guideline for every condition but to achieve the simplest effective regimen — and these tools provide the evidence base for doing so safely."
                }
              ],
